{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this production plan — should I maximize total profit (unit price minus raw material cost minus the equipment operating costs, with the operating costs treated as fixed charges incurred whenever a machine is used at all), or maximize total revenue, or something else?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting mutually exclusive options within one sentence."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there a demand or order quantity for each product (I, II, III) that the plan must meet, or are the production quantities free to choose (subject only to the machine-hour limits and the requirement that each unit goes through both A and B)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding production quantities: whether they are fixed by demand or free variables. Although it lists three products, it asks for the status of the quantities for all of them in a single binary choice (fixed vs. free), which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Do you want me to allow producing zero units of a product (i.e., simply not make it if it doesn't pay), or is there a minimum production requirement for any of the products?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding production constraints (allowing zero production vs. enforcing a minimum), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Does \"used at all\" mean the machine is considered used (and the full charge incurred) if even a single unit is processed on it, or is there some minimum utilization threshold below which the charge is not incurred?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy definition regarding the trigger for incurring fixed operating costs, presenting two mutually exclusive options for the same underlying rule."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the fixed operating cost of a machine, is the charge incurred based on whether any product is processed on that machine for either procedure A or procedure B, or is it incurred separately for each procedure (i.e., a machine could be \"used\" for A and \"used\" for B independently, incurring the charge once per procedure it is used for)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a specific policy choice regarding how fixed operating costs are triggered (per machine usage vs. per procedure usage)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For a given product, can different units be split across different machines for procedure A (e.g., some units of Product I on A1 and some on A2), or must all units of a given product use the same machine for a given procedure?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether units of a product can be split across machines for a specific procedure. Although it mentions procedure A as an example, the core inquiry is a single policy choice about machine assignment granularity."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since units can be split across machines, can the split be fractional (e.g., 2.5 units of Product I on A1 and 3.5 on A2), or must the number of units assigned to each machine be a whole number?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether unit assignments must be integers or can be fractional."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the raw material cost incurred once per unit of finished product (i.e., one unit of raw material per unit of product, regardless of which machines process it), or is it incurred per processing step (so a unit going through both A and B would incur the raw material cost twice)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding how raw material costs are applied (per finished unit vs. per processing step), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is this the total available time for the machine over the entire planning period (i.e., the sum of processing times for all units on that machine must not exceed this number), or is it a per-period limit that applies to each period separately?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the scope of the 'Effective Machine Hours' constraint (total vs. per-period), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The processing times in the table (e.g., 5, 10, 7, etc.) — are these in the same units as the \"Effective Machine Hours\" (i.e., if a machine has 6000 effective hours, and a product takes 5 units of time on that machine, then 6000/5 = 1200 units could be processed)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the unit consistency between processing times and effective machine hours."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For Product II, which can be processed on A1 or A2 for procedure A, and only on B1 for procedure B — if a unit of Product II is processed on A1 for procedure A, does it still need to go through B1 for procedure B, or could it skip procedure B entirely?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a specific policy choice regarding the necessity of procedure B for Product II."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For Product III, which can only be processed on A2 for procedure A and on B2 for procedure B — is it possible for a unit of Product III to be processed on A2 for procedure A but then not go through B2 for procedure B (i.e., be left incomplete), or must every unit that starts on A2 also complete on B2?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether Product III units can be left incomplete after procedure A or must always complete procedure B."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For Product I, which can be processed on A1 or A2 for procedure A, and on B1, B2, or B3 for procedure B — can a unit of Product I be processed on A1 for procedure A and then on B3 for procedure B, or is there any pairing restriction between which A machine and which B machine a unit can use?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether specific machine pairings are allowed or restricted for Product I."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "If a machine is used for both procedure A and procedure B (e.g., B1 is used for Product I and Product II in procedure B), is the fixed charge incurred only once for that machine, or once per procedure it is used for?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy decision regarding how fixed charges are allocated when a machine is shared across procedures."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any machines that can be used for both procedure A and procedure B, or is each machine dedicated to only one procedure?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding machine flexibility, presented as a binary choice (shared vs. dedicated), which constitutes one independent question."
}

